untime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NLDE1qcGfZQ9WfKB8wRdHp", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["honor_retry_after", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379436, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NLDE1qcGfZQ9WfKB8wRdHp", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383465, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said it uses banker's rounding. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. When I tried to look up FIN-212 itself, the advisory system didn't recognise it, so I went by the test and the code comment for what's required.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ASjzCmxqnRbgmii7gHYhjd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017q3HhyTu1HcUboy7PbjPqb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Bn4MTJVgwMjVLEBh8gDkip", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QUtDCdQozyaPBoVoiunFwv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011G1fzJoLpuwo4NAXWFqfCX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Bh3YGYAKyYkiUxmo48f6Ki", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-banker-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SS6CpStSQyfPBYzvxXxJem", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NLDE1qcGfZQ9WfKB8wRdHp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-banker-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though its docstring says half-even.\n\nThis PR switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description said it uses banker's rounding. So `2.665` came out as `2.67` instead of the `2.66` the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit (`08d3cd5986`).\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval. When I tried to look up FIN-212 itself, the advisory system didn't recognise it, so I went by the test and the code comment for what's required.", "type": "text"}]}]}